# ==========================================================================
#  O45  Universal restrictions: types the values, and is true of nothing
# ==========================================================================
#
#  DECIDES
#    'A bookshop stocks only works' is written with owl:allValuesFrom,
#    which types every value of bs:stocks on a bookshop as a Work and is
#    trivially satisfied by a shop that stocks nothing.
#
#  WHY
#    The universal restriction is the set of things all of whose bs:stocks
#    values are Works, including the things that have no values at all. Put
#    bs:Bookshop under it and the reasoner types every stocked thing as a
#    Work: this is a local range, and both HermiT and the RL closure
#    produce the triple. A shop that stocks nothing satisfies it vacuously,
#    which surprises people who read 'only' as 'at least one and only'.
#
#    gist's fifth rule says what a subclass universal is good for: it adds
#    information about the class without inferring anything into it. And
#    rules one and two say what an equivalence to a universal is good for,
#    which is inferring into the complement: since nothing can be shown to
#    have only Work values under the open world, no individual is ever
#    classified into the class, but one with a non-Work value can be
#    classified out of it. That is a subtle tool and o47 uses its cousin.
#
#    The everyday use is the range you cannot declare globally. bs:stocks
#    on a bookshop points at works; the same property on a library, if the
#    vocabulary had one, might point at editions. A global rdfs:range would
#    type both; the local universal types only the bookshop's values.
#
#  DIAGRAM
#       bs:Bookshop rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:onProperty bs:stocks ; owl:allValuesFrom bs:Work ]
#
#       set reading:  B is a subset of { x : for every y, stocks(x, y) implies y in W }
#
#       bt:shop-inkwell bs:stocks bt:thing     =>  bt:thing a bs:Work         (HermiT and the RL closure)
#       bt:shop-errata stocks nothing          =>  satisfied, vacuously
#
#       a local range: types the values of this property on this class only
#
#  WHAT TO TAKE AWAY
#    - allValuesFrom types the values. It is a range scoped to one class.
#    - 'Only' includes 'none'. A thing with no values satisfies every
#      universal restriction.
#    - Under the open world nothing can be proved to have only such
#      values, so an equivalence to a universal never infers into the
#      class. It can infer out of it.
#
#  TRY IT
#    Show Facts: bt:thing is a bs:Work. Add a second value that is declared
#    a bs:Person, with Person disjoint from Work, and the RL closure will
#    type it a Work anyway; HermiT will call the file inconsistent. Same
#    axiom, two engines, o43's lesson again.
#
#  CORNER    referent
#  RUNS IN   the browser
#  LOAD IT   https://semantechs.co.uk/turtle-editor-viewer/?dot=https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fpwin%2FOntology_Course%2Fmain%2Flessons%2F07-owl%2Fo45-universal-restrictions-types-the-values-and-is-true-of-nothing.ttl
#  SOURCES   OWL 2 Primer 5.2 Property Restrictions: universal quantification
#            https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-primer/#Property_Restrictions
#            gist Style Guide: OWL restrictions, the eleven rules
#            https://github.com/semanticarts/gist/blob/develop/docs/gistStyleGuide.md#owl-restrictions
#  MEASURED  parses, 14 triples; 2 classes, 1 object property, 2 individuals; OWL 2 DL in profile; HermiT: consistent, 1 inferred; RL closure +1
# ==========================================================================

@prefix bt:   <https://example.org/bookshop-trail/> .
@prefix bs:   <https://example.org/bookshop-trail/schema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

skos:prefLabel      a owl:AnnotationProperty .
skos:definition     a owl:AnnotationProperty .
skos:editorialNote  a owl:AnnotationProperty .

bs:Work      a owl:Class .
bs:Bookshop  a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty bs:stocks ; owl:allValuesFrom bs:Work ] .
bs:stocks    a owl:ObjectProperty .

bt:shop-inkwell  a bs:Bookshop ; bs:stocks bt:thing .
bt:thing         skos:prefLabel "Something the shop stocks; the axiom will say what"@en .
bt:shop-errata   a bs:Bookshop .
